\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Conceptually, the PSL will be made up of four components: the NRPO, two neoVAN-4S-HP amplifiers and the PMC cavity. The NPRO provides seed light with good noise characteristics. These noise characteristics are preserved by the amplifiers, so the resulting beam will have high power and low noise. As the linewidth of the PMC $\sim 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\rm  {MHz}$, it filters away light in higher order modes and RF intensity noise so a quiet, spatially pure mode can be sent to the interferometer.\relax }}{38}{figure.caption.10}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapterconcept}{{3.1}{38}{Conceptually, the PSL will be made up of four components: the NRPO, two neoVAN-4S-HP amplifiers and the PMC cavity. The NPRO provides seed light with good noise characteristics. These noise characteristics are preserved by the amplifiers, so the resulting beam will have high power and low noise. As the linewidth of the PMC $\sim 1\,\rm {MHz}$, it filters away light in higher order modes and RF intensity noise so a quiet, spatially pure mode can be sent to the interferometer.\relax }{figure.caption.10}{}}
