\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.19}{\ignorespaces Sketch of the amplitude stabilisation servo. By measuring the ratio of the signal at point B and point A, the transfer function of all the parts in the servo (apart from the $\times 1$ adding stage) can be measured (see Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:ligolaserchapterdaigramfortfmeasurement}).\relax }}{73}{figure.caption.28}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapteroltfmeasurement}{{3.19}{73}{Sketch of the amplitude stabilisation servo. By measuring the ratio of the signal at point B and point A, the transfer function of all the parts in the servo (apart from the $\times 1$ adding stage) can be measured (see Figure~\ref {fig:ligolaserchapterdaigramfortfmeasurement}).\relax }{figure.caption.28}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.20}{\ignorespaces The open-loop transfer function was measured using the layout shown in Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:ligolaserchapteroltfmeasurement}. The unity gain point is at 48\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\kilo \hertz } with 70\si {\degree } of phase margin. The shaping of the servo is $1/f$ at the unity gain point, but to achieve higher gain at low frequency, the servo has a $/f^3$ slope between 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz---5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}kHz. The measurement saturated below 100\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz. The model and measurement do not agree well below a few kHz due to the measurement saturating.\relax }}{74}{figure.caption.29}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapteropenlooptransferfunction}{{3.20}{74}{The open-loop transfer function was measured using the layout shown in Figure~\ref {fig:ligolaserchapteroltfmeasurement}. The unity gain point is at 48\,\si {\kilo \hertz } with 70\si {\degree } of phase margin. The shaping of the servo is $1/f$ at the unity gain point, but to achieve higher gain at low frequency, the servo has a $/f^3$ slope between 10\,Hz---5\,kHz. The measurement saturated below 100\,Hz. The model and measurement do not agree well below a few kHz due to the measurement saturating.\relax }{figure.caption.29}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.21}{\ignorespaces Block diagram of the components in the the intensity stabilisation servo. The transfer function of each block is described in Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:ligolaserchapterservomodel} and Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:ligolaserchapterservomodel}. The overall gain of the servo depends on a variable gain chip and the amount of light on the photodiode. The shaping of each block is indicated below it.\relax }}{75}{figure.caption.30}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapteroltfmodelblockdiagram}{{3.21}{75}{Block diagram of the components in the the intensity stabilisation servo. The transfer function of each block is described in Section~\ref {sec:ligolaserchapterservomodel} and Table~\ref {tab:ligolaserchapterservomodel}. The overall gain of the servo depends on a variable gain chip and the amount of light on the photodiode. The shaping of each block is indicated below it.\relax }{figure.caption.30}{}}
