\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Sketch showing the parts of the aLIGO detectors discussed in this chapter. A more complete sketch is shown in Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:ligolayout}. The angles and lengths are exaggerated for clarity. Light from the arm cavities is incident upon the beam splitter (BS). As BS is wedged, the light going towards the SRC comes out an an angle. Differential arm length signals encoded onto this light are directed towards SR3, SR2, and then the SRM. Between the SRM and the OMC, there are optics for steering and mode matching (OM1-3). Finally, to strip away junk light, the light enters the OMC. The light emerging from the OMC is detected by photodiodes.\relax }}{96}{figure.caption.40}}
\newlabel{fig:beamparameterchapterligolayout}{{4.1}{96}{Sketch showing the parts of the aLIGO detectors discussed in this chapter. A more complete sketch is shown in Figure~\ref {fig:ligolayout}. The angles and lengths are exaggerated for clarity. Light from the arm cavities is incident upon the beam splitter (BS). As BS is wedged, the light going towards the SRC comes out an an angle. Differential arm length signals encoded onto this light are directed towards SR3, SR2, and then the SRM. Between the SRM and the OMC, there are optics for steering and mode matching (OM1-3). Finally, to strip away junk light, the light enters the OMC. The light emerging from the OMC is detected by photodiodes.\relax }{figure.caption.40}{}}
