\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces A coherent state $\mathinner {|{\alpha }\delimiter "526930B }$, enters port $a$ of a beam splitter. A signal $\mathinner {|{\Psi }\delimiter "526930B }$ enters port $b$. These two beams interfere, resulting in photons being detected at the $c$ and $d$ ports. The two photocurrents are subtracted, and the signal that is produced is proportional to an arbitrary quadrature of the state $\mathinner {|{\Psi }\delimiter "526930B }$; the difference in the signals at the $c$ and $d$ ports is given by Equation\nobreakspace  {}(\ref  {eq:bhd_signal}). The quadrature of the state $\mathinner {|{\Psi }\delimiter "526930B }$ that is observed depends on the homodyne angle, $\phi $. \relax }}{135}{figure.caption.58}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterbhdsketch}{{5.1}{135}{A coherent state $\ket {\alpha }$, enters port $a$ of a beam splitter. A signal $\ket {\Psi }$ enters port $b$. These two beams interfere, resulting in photons being detected at the $c$ and $d$ ports. The two photocurrents are subtracted, and the signal that is produced is proportional to an arbitrary quadrature of the state $\ket {\Psi }$; the difference in the signals at the $c$ and $d$ ports is given by Equation~(\ref {eq:bhd_signal}). The quadrature of the state $\ket {\Psi }$ that is observed depends on the homodyne angle, $\phi $. \relax }{figure.caption.58}{}}
