\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Astigmatism is a source of loss. When designing the layout shown in Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:bhdforligochapterlayout5f}, the AOI for the curved mirrors was altered to explore how sensitive it was to astigmatism. Using Equation (\ref  {eq:bhd_for_ligo_mm_loss}), the loss was computed. This effect is negligible up to 10\si {\degree } after which it starts to become significant compared to the losses summarised in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:HAM6_losses}.\relax }}{157}{figure.caption.66}}
