\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.7}{\ignorespaces The amplitude spectral density of the difference between the two photodiode's signals ($\rm  {S_{BHD}}$) is shown in blue. The peak at 6033\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz was injected to demonstrate this measurement corresponds to differential arm length modulations. The expected shot noise is based on Equation\nobreakspace  {}(\ref  {eq:MZ_chapter_shot_noise_level}), and this is shown by the dashed red line. The noise measured at frequencies above 5500\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz is within 5\% of the expected shot noise. Below 5500\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz, acoustic noise limited the Mach-Zehnder's sensitivity. This plot is for emphasising the shot noise limit of the measurement in metres; for an analysis of the noise below 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}kHz, see Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:mzchapterfullnoisespectrumwithcouplings}.\relax }}{228}{figure.caption.96}}
\newlabel{fig:mzchapterfullnoisespectrum}{{8.7}{228}{The amplitude spectral density of the difference between the two photodiode's signals ($\rm {S_{BHD}}$) is shown in blue. The peak at 6033\,Hz was injected to demonstrate this measurement corresponds to differential arm length modulations. The expected shot noise is based on Equation~(\ref {eq:MZ_chapter_shot_noise_level}), and this is shown by the dashed red line. The noise measured at frequencies above 5500\,Hz is within 5\% of the expected shot noise. Below 5500\,Hz, acoustic noise limited the Mach-Zehnder's sensitivity. This plot is for emphasising the shot noise limit of the measurement in metres; for an analysis of the noise below 1\,kHz, see Figure~\ref {fig:mzchapterfullnoisespectrumwithcouplings}.\relax }{figure.caption.96}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.8}{\ignorespaces The amplitude spectral density of the difference between the two photodiode's signals ($\rm  {S_{BHD}}$) is shown in blue. The frequency noise that couples via a difference in path lengths between the two arms was estimated, and this is shown in green. The estimated spectrum due to 300\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}fW of scattered light is shown in yellow.\relax }}{229}{figure.caption.97}}
\newlabel{fig:mzchapterfullnoisespectrumwithcouplings}{{8.8}{229}{The amplitude spectral density of the difference between the two photodiode's signals ($\rm {S_{BHD}}$) is shown in blue. The frequency noise that couples via a difference in path lengths between the two arms was estimated, and this is shown in green. The estimated spectrum due to 300\,fW of scattered light is shown in yellow.\relax }{figure.caption.97}{}}
