\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A.15}{\ignorespaces The noise of the photocurrent produced by the P5968 as a function of bias. The photocurrent due to thermal radiation was expected to be 5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\micro \ampere }, and the noise of the photocurrent made by the P5986 at sufficiently low bias reaches the expected shot noise for this current. The benchmark noise corresponding to a 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\milli \ampere } photocurrent is also shown.\relax }}{258}{figure.caption.119}}
